🌐 2. Shodan — Internet ka Search Engine
6

Sabse pehle Shodan.

Normal Google kya search karta hai?

Web pages
Articles
Images
Videos
Documents

Shodan ka focus different hai.

Shodan kya karta hai?

Shodan internet par publicly reachable devices/services ko continuously scan/index karta hai.

For example:

Web servers
Routers
Cameras
VPN gateways
Industrial systems
Databases
IoT devices

So tum roughly ye dekh sakte ho:

IP
   ↓
Port
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Software
   ↓
Version
Example

Suppose Shodan mein tum search karte ho:

apache 2.4.1

Shodan un internet-facing systems ko dhoondh sakta hai jo apne response/banner mein Apache 2.4.1 advertise kar rahe hain.

Iska security use kya hai?

Suppose:

Apache 2.4.1
       ↓
Known vulnerability
       ↓
CVE
       ↓
Security assessment

To security researcher ko idea mil sakta hai ki kis type ke systems potentially affected ho sakte hain.

⚠️ Lekin important distinction:

Shodan result milna ≠ system hack karne ki permission.

Publicly visible hone ka matlab publicly attackable/authorized nahi hota.

🔎 3. Shodan Filters

Ye part important hai.

Shodan ke paas search filters hain.

country

Country restrict karne ke liye:

country:IE

Matlab Ireland ke results.

port

Specific port search karna:

port:22

Yaani SSH-related exposed services.

Port:

80
443
22
3389

etc.

org

Kisi organisation/ASN ke scope mein search.

Example:

AS7224

ASN basically ek network/organisation ke IP ranges ka identifier samajh lo.

Simple analogy:

ASN = Internet par organisation ka network-area identifier.

hostname

Specific hostname/domain ke liye:

hostname:example.com

Ye useful hai jab tum authorized organisation/domain ke internet-facing assets investigate kar rahe ho.

🦠 4. VirusTotal
5

Ab aao VirusTotal par.

VirusTotal ko simple language mein samjho:

“Ek jagah par multiple security engines se suspicious file/URL/domain ko check karna.”

Suppose tumhare paas file hai:

invoice_payment.exe

Tumhe doubt hai:

“Bhai ye genuine invoice software hai ya malware?”

VirusTotal mein file/hash/URL/domain etc. ke basis par information mil sakti hai.

Multiple security vendors apna verdict dete hain.

Example conceptual result:

Vendor A     → Malicious
Vendor B     → Malicious
Vendor C     → Clean
Vendor D     → Malicious
Vendor E     → Clean

Agar:

70 engines
↓
45 detect
↓
25 don't detect

to iska matlab:

45 security vendors ne suspicious/malicious identify kiya.

But ek important lesson:

❌ VirusTotal = 100% truth

Nahi.

A detection consensus useful evidence hai, final proof nahi.

False positives ho sakte hain.

🧪 5. TryHackMe ka VirusTotal Practical

Tumhare room mein practical diya hai:

invoice_payment.exe

Tumhe TryHackMe ke simulated VirusTotal/TryDetectMe environment mein search karna hai.

Steps ka meaning:

Step 1

Search:

invoice_payment.exe
Step 2

Security vendors ka result dekho.

Step 3

Count karo:

Kitne vendors ne dangerous/malicious identify kiya?

Bas wahi answer room mein submit karna hai.

Ye practical real VirusTotal par nahi, TryHackMe simulation mein hai.

🛡️ 6. CVE — Vulnerability ka Universal ID

Ab cybersecurity ka bahut important concept.

CVE = Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures

Simple language:

CVE ek known security vulnerability ko diya gaya unique identification number hai.

Example:

CVE-2025-55182

Isko parts mein dekho:

CVE
│
├── 2025  → year
│
└── 55182 → vulnerability identifier

Matlab jab security industry mein log us vulnerability ki baat karenge, sabko pata rahega ki exactly kaunsi vulnerability ki baat ho rahi hai.

🎯 CVE ki zarurat kyun?

Suppose ek researcher bolta hai:

“Apache mein ek serious remote vulnerability hai.”

Vendor A usko kuch naam deta hai.

Researcher B kuch aur naam deta hai.

Security tool kuch aur naam use karta hai.

Confusion. 😵‍💫

CVE ek common identifier provide karta hai:

CVE-202X-XXXXX

Ab everyone same vulnerability ko refer kar sakta hai.

🔥 7. CVE vs CVSS

Ye dono confuse mat karna.

CVE

“Kaunsi vulnerability?”

Example:

CVE-2025-XXXXX
CVSS

“Vulnerability kitni serious hai?”

Conceptually:

CVE
 ↓
Vulnerability identify
 ↓
CVSS
 ↓
Severity/risk understand

CVSS factors mein exploitability aur impact jaise characteristics consider hote hain.

Generally severity categories:

None
Low
Medium
High
Critical

Security teams often higher-risk vulnerabilities ko priority dete hain.

💥 8. Vulnerability ko naam bhi mil sakta hai

Kabhi-kabhi serious vulnerabilities ko memorable naam mil jata hai.

For example:

Heartbleed
Log4Shell

Naam yaad rakhna easy hota hai.

Lekin underlying vulnerability ka formal identifier phir bhi CVE ho sakta hai.

So:

Nickname
   ↓
Human-friendly


CVE
   ↓
Official/common identifier
🧨 9. ExploitDB kya hai?

Text mein ExploitDB ka mention hai.

Isko simple samjho:

ExploitDB ek database hai jahan known vulnerabilities se related exploit/PoC information mil sakti hai.

Suppose tumhare paas:

CVE-XXXX-XXXXX

Ab tum investigate karna chahte ho:

“Kya is vulnerability ka public proof-of-concept available hai?”

Exploit databases useful ho sakte hain.

🧪 10. PoC kya hota hai?

PoC = Proof of Concept

Simple:

Kisi vulnerability ko practically demonstrate karne wala code/example.

Suppose vulnerability theoretically kehti hai:

Software X
     ↓
Input validation problem
     ↓
Potential security impact

Researcher ek PoC bana sakta hai jo demonstrate kare ki vulnerability actually trigger ho sakti hai.

But bhai, yahan ek important professional habit:

PoC mila ≠ blindly execute karo.

Especially GitHub/ExploitDB se downloaded code.

Pehle:

Read code
↓
Understand what it does
↓
Check source/reputation
↓
Use isolated lab
↓
Only authorized target
