🧠 Real-world Cybersecurity Investigation Example

Ab maan lo tumhare authorized lab mein server hai:

192.168.1.50

Nmap se tum discover karte ho:

22/tcp   SSH
80/tcp   HTTP
443/tcp  HTTPS

Web service identify karne par pata chalta hai:

Apache 2.4.x

Ab tumhara workflow ho sakta hai:

Nmap
  ↓
Service identification
  ↓
Apache version
  ↓
Search vulnerability databases
  ↓
Relevant CVEs
  ↓
CVSS severity
  ↓
Official vendor advisory
  ↓
Possible PoC/research
  ↓
Validate ONLY in authorized lab

Aur agar suspicious file milti hai:

invoice.exe
      ↓
Hash
      ↓
VirusTotal
      ↓
Vendor detections
      ↓
Threat intelligence

Aur agar internet-facing asset research karna hai:

Domain / IP
      ↓
Shodan
      ↓
Publicly exposed services
      ↓
Service/version information
🎯 Tumhe is chapter se kya yaad rakhna hai?
Tool/Resource	Simple meaning	Kab use karna
Shodan	Internet-connected systems/services ka search engine	Exposure/asset research
VirusTotal	Multiple security engines ka analysis platform	Suspicious files/URLs/domains
CVE	Vulnerability ka unique ID	Vulnerability identify/reference
CVSS	Vulnerability severity/risk score	Priority samajhna
ExploitDB	Public exploit/PoC database	Vulnerability research
Official Docs	Tool ka authoritative manual	Correct usage
man	Linux terminal documentation	Commands/options samajhna
GitHub	Code + research repositories	Tools, PoCs, research
Ek line mein poora chapter:

“Cybersecurity mein hacker ya defender banne ke liye sirf tools chalana nahi, balki information ko efficiently discover, verify aur interpret karna bhi aana chahiye.”

Aur tumhare current learning path ke hisaab se Shodan + CVE + CVSS + VirusTotal + man pages ko achhe se samajhna bahut useful hai. Ye baad mein Nmap, Wireshark, SOC investigation aur vulnerability assessment sab jagah baar-baar kaam aayega.
